---
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
import ProjectTags from "../../components/ProjectTags.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout>
  <section class="mb-12">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4">
          <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold">MapLaser</h1>
          <a href="https://github.com/MatthewTHutchinson/maplaser" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="MapLaser on GitHub" title="View MapLaser on GitHub" class="inline-flex size-11 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded hover:bg-gray-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 19c-4.3 1.4 -4.3 -2.5 -6 -3m12 5v-3.5c0 -1 .1 -1.4 -.5 -2c2.8 -.3 5.5 -1.4 5.5 -6a4.6 4.6 0 0 0 -1.3 -3.2a4.2 4.2 0 0 0 -.1 -3.2s-1.1 -.3 -3.5 1.3a12.3 12.3 0 0 0 -6.2 0c-2.4 -1.6 -3.5 -1.3 -3.5 -1.3a4.2 4.2 0 0 0 -.1 3.2a4.6 4.6 0 0 0 -1.3 3.2c0 4.6 2.7 5.7 5.5 6c-.6 .6 -.6 1.2 -.5 2v3.5" /></svg>
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 max-w-3xl">
          I built a local web app that turns geographic data into layered SVG maps for laser cutting and terrain models for 3D printing. It grew out of city and campus maps I made at the UCLA Makerspace, where preparing roads, aligning layers, and keeping small details sturdy took substantial manual cleanup.
        </p>
        <ProjectTags />
      </div>

      <figure class="w-full sm:w-2/3 mx-auto">
        <img
          src="/media/makerspace work/sf-map-1.jpeg"
          alt="Laser-cut San Francisco map"
          class="w-full aspect-square object-cover object-[50%_46%]"
        />
        <figcaption class="px-3 py-1.5 text-xs text-gray-400">San Francisco map, made at the UCLA Makerspace.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12 space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">What I Built</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
      <li>Built a Python/FastAPI backend with a Leaflet map interface and Three.js model preview, including worldwide place search, movable and rotatable crops, and rectangular, circular, or hexagonal outputs.</li>
      <li>Combined OpenStreetMap roads and buildings with elevation tiles and imported GPX routes. A shared local projection, crop, and physical scale keep the exported layers aligned.</li>
      <li>Separated laser and 3D generation so vector-only work skips elevation fetching and mesh construction. Recipes preserve the selected area and fabrication settings for reuse.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12 space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Laser Maps</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Road classes have independent filters and physical widths. The generator buffers and merges road geometry into closed outlines, retaining bridge roads instead of clipping them to land. Editable SVGs keep roads grouped by class; separate cut exports merge intersections and an optional supporting frame to avoid duplicate cut lines.</p>
    <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">A review bundle contains aligned base and road SVGs, an editable reference, and checks for disconnected pieces and laser-bed fit. Margins expand the board without rescaling the map. The original NYC pipeline also combines detailed shoreline and transit layers for compositions finished in Illustrator.</p>
    <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 pt-4">
      <figure>
        <a href="/media/maplaser/nyc-map-2.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open New York City map at full size">
          <img src="/media/maplaser/nyc-map-2.png" alt="New York City map composition and its Illustrator layer structure" class="w-full aspect-[4/3] object-contain bg-white" loading="lazy" />
        </a>
        <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500">New York City composition in Illustrator.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <a href="/media/maplaser/la-map-1.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open Los Angeles map at full size">
          <img src="/media/maplaser/la-map-1.png" alt="Los Angeles map showing roads, coastline, waterways, and terrain contours" class="w-full aspect-[4/3] object-contain bg-white" loading="lazy" />
        </a>
        <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500">Los Angeles map.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12 space-y-4">
    <h2 id="3d-terrain" class="text-2xl font-bold">3D Terrain</h2>
    <figure>
      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-[1.76fr_1fr] items-start">
        <a href="/media/maplaser/la-3d-3.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open Los Angeles 3D terrain workspace at full size">
          <img src="/media/maplaser/la-3d-3.png" alt="MapLaser workspace showing a rectangular Los Angeles terrain model with downtown buildings, roads, and the Los Angeles River" width="2386" height="1644" class="w-full h-auto" loading="lazy" />
        </a>
        <a href="/media/maplaser/la-map-3.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the selected Los Angeles map area at full size">
          <img src="/media/maplaser/la-map-3.png" alt="Los Angeles map with a rectangular crop covering downtown, Echo Park, and the Los Angeles River" width="1258" height="1528" class="w-full h-auto" loading="lazy" />
        </a>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500">Los Angeles terrain model and selected map area. Building heights are exaggerated; missing source heights use an estimated value.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <a href="/media/maplaser/la-3d-1.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the alternate Los Angeles 3D terrain view at full size">
        <img src="/media/maplaser/la-3d-1.png" alt="Alternate view of the Los Angeles terrain model, showing downtown building heights and the surrounding road network" width="2366" height="1642" class="w-full h-auto" loading="lazy" />
      </a>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500">Downtown Los Angeles from another angle.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The 3D workflow samples elevation into a terrain surface with adjustable exaggeration, base thickness, and grid resolution. Roads, building footprints, and GPX routes can be included on the surface. The generator closes the sides and bottom, validates the mesh, and exports a single-body STL or 3MF for slicer review.</p>
    <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Elevation comes from AWS Terrain Tiles, map features from OpenStreetMap through Overpass, and place search from Photon.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12 space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Fabrication Constraints</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Road widths are set in output millimeters rather than taken as surveyed street widths. This lets a small map retain roads that would otherwise be too delicate to cut. In 3D, the terrain grid limits how much road and building detail survives; vector exports bypass that grid.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">San Francisco Map Series</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
      {[
        "sf-map-2.JPG",
        "sf-map-3.JPG",
        "sf-map-4.JPG",
        "sf-map-5.jpg",
        "sf-map-6.jpg",
      ].map((filename) => (
        <figure class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 shadow-sm">
          <img
            src={`/media/makerspace work/${filename}`}
            alt="Laser-cut San Francisco map detail"
            class="w-full h-auto"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </figure>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">UCLA Map Series</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
      {[
        "ucla-map.JPG",
        "ucla-map-2.jpg",
        "ucla-map-3.JPG",
        "ucla-map-4.JPG",
        "ucla-map-5.jpg",
      ].map((filename) => (
        <figure class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 shadow-sm">
          <img
            src={`/media/makerspace work/${filename}`}
            alt="Laser-cut UCLA campus map detail"
            class="w-full h-auto"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </figure>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</ProjectLayout>
